# Design Tokens

## Two-Layer Color System

### Layer 1: Primitives (`@theme/primitives.ts`)
Raw color values with numeric scale. Named `ColorName + Scale` in PascalCase.
```
brand100 ... brand900
neutral100 ... neutral900
red100 ... red900
blue100 ... blue900
green100 ... green900
orange100 ... orange900
purple300, purple500
yellow300, yellow500
cyan300, cyan500
violet300, violet500
white, black
```
**Rule**: Never reference primitives directly inside component files. Only themes and token files may reference primitives.

### Layer 2: Semantic Tokens (`@theme/tokens.ts`)
Colors by role/usage. These are the only colors components should use.

```ts
// Accessed via useTheme()
const { tokens } = useTheme();

// Background
tokens.bgWinter          // Main screen background (winter theme)
tokens.bgSummer          // Main screen background (summer theme)
tokens.bgAi              // AI feature backgrounds
tokens.bgSurface         // Modal windows, bottom sheets
tokens.bgOnSurface       // Cards and elements on surfaces
tokens.bgCard            // Card background

// Interactive (buttons, toggles, interactive elements)
tokens.intPrimary        // Primary interactive — teal brand
tokens.intPrimaryPressed // Primary pressed state
tokens.intSecondary      // Secondary interactive — light fill
tokens.intSecondaryPressed
tokens.intDisabled       // All disabled interactive elements

// Text
tokens.textOnInt         // Text on interactive elements (white on teal)
tokens.textOnIntSecondary
tokens.textOnCard        // Primary text on cards
tokens.textOnCardSecondary
tokens.textOnBgOnSurface // Primary text on surface backgrounds
tokens.textOnBgOnSurfaceSecondary
tokens.textDisabled      // Disabled text

// Icon
tokens.iconOnInt
tokens.iconOnIntSecondary
tokens.iconOnCard
tokens.iconOnCardSecondary
tokens.iconDisabled

// Strokes & Dividers
tokens.strokeOnSurface
tokens.dividerOnSurface
```

## Theme Switching
Themes in `@theme/themes/`. Currently: `winter` (default), `summer`.
`useTheme()` returns the active theme's token set. Components are theme-agnostic.

**Do not hard-code any theme-conditional logic in components.**
If a component looks different per-theme, that difference must be expressed through tokens.

## Typography Tokens
Variant names map directly to Figma token names (camelCase conversion):
```
Figma: body-1-highlight → Code: 'body1Highlight'
Figma: cta-large        → Code: 'ctaLarge'
Figma: caption-label    → Code: 'captionLabel'
```

All text must go through `<AppTypography variant="body1" />` component.
Never use raw `<Text>` in component files.

Full variant list:
```
number1
display1, display2
title1, title2, title3
body1Highlight, body1TinyHighlight, body1, body1Tiny
body2Highlight, body2TinyHighlight, body2, body2Tiny
captionHighlight, captionRegular, captionLabel
ctaLarge, ctaRegular, ctaSmall
```

## Spacing Tokens
```ts
import { spacing } from '@theme/spacing';

spacing.tiny      // 4
spacing.small     // 8
spacing.medium    // 12
spacing.large     // 16
spacing.extraLarge // 20
spacing.xxLarge   // 24
spacing.xxxLarge  // 32
```

## Validation Checklist
When creating or reviewing a component, verify:
- [ ] No hardcoded hex colors anywhere in the component file
- [ ] No hardcoded spacing numbers — using `spacing.*` everywhere
- [ ] All text through `AppTypography`, never raw `Text`
- [ ] `allowFontScaling={false}` is set (handled by AppTypography)
- [ ] Colors reference `tokens.*` from `useTheme()`, not primitives

## Adding New Tokens
When Figma introduces a new semantic color:
1. Add it to `ColorTokens` interface in `@theme/tokens.ts`
2. Add value to `winterTokens` in `@theme/themes/winter.ts`
3. Add value to `summerTokens` in `@theme/themes/summer.ts`
4. Never add a token to only one theme — both must stay in sync
